  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145942",
      "title": "Writing Our First API Route",
      "lectureOrder": 318,
      "videoOrder": 295,
      "sourceHash": "56417d03950d7ffcc27c2b5ff21dfeeb93cfb43457a7c2c2cc97b48c263c44bb",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.591,
          "end": 5.52,
          "en": "Now, how do we add our own API routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.52,
          "end": 8.11,
          "en": "to a next.js application though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.11,
          "end": 12.01,
          "en": "For this, I got a brand new next.js project for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.01,
          "end": 14.97,
          "en": "You'll find it attached to this lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.97,
          "end": 17.98,
          "en": "You can extract it, run npm install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.98,
          "end": 19.54,
          "en": "and then once you did that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.54,
          "end": 21.659,
          "en": "npm run dev to start it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.659,
          "end": 26.27,
          "en": "But this application will now not be about our pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.27,
          "end": 28.94,
          "en": "at least not the standard pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.94,
          "end": 29.83,
          "en": "Indeed, there only,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.83,
          "end": 32.38,
          "en": "is one page in that starting project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.38,
          "end": 34.6,
          "en": "and that's a dummy homepage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.6,
          "end": 37.53,
          "en": "which just says \"The homepage\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.53,
          "end": 40.22,
          "en": "Now, of course we can visit this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.22,
          "end": 43.39,
          "en": "through local host 3000, but again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.39,
          "end": 45.69,
          "en": "this course module will not be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.69,
          "end": 47.94,
          "en": "about creating pages like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.94,
          "end": 51.21,
          "en": "Instead it is about this API routes feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.21,
          "end": 54.26,
          "en": "which is a feature built into next.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.26,
          "end": 58.6,
          "en": "We can add our own API endpoints to next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.6,
          "end": 63.19,
          "en": "by simply creating a new sub folder inside of pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.19,
          "end": 67.81,
          "en": "So, inside of this pages directory, we create a sub folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.81,
          "end": 72.37,
          "en": "and that sub folder has to be called API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.37,
          "end": 74.95,
          "en": "Now up to this point, those file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.95,
          "end": 77.41499999999999,
          "en": "and folder names were mostly up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.41499999999999,
          "end": 79.42,
          "en": "This is now not up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.42,
          "end": 84.42,
          "en": "This has to be called API because that's a special folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.51,
          "end": 87.86,
          "en": "which will be recognized by next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.86,
          "end": 91.56,
          "en": "and any pages if you wanna call them like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.56,
          "end": 93.13,
          "en": "which you set up inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.13,
          "end": 97.49000000000001,
          "en": "of that API folder will be treated in a special way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.49000000000001,
          "end": 100.57300000000001,
          "en": "So let's add a page inside of the API folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.97800000000001,
          "end": 103.68,
          "en": "In there, you can add pages just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.68,
          "end": 106.89,
          "en": "as you can add them anywhere else in the pages folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.89,
          "end": 108.02000000000001,
          "en": "So you can pick names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.02000000000001,
          "end": 111.58,
          "en": "of your choice index.js to handle the requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.58,
          "end": 114.65,
          "en": "which are just directed at /API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.65,
          "end": 119.14,
          "en": "or to get started here, feedback.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.14,
          "end": 122.11,
          "en": "Let's name it feedback.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.11,
          "end": 126.26,
          "en": "So now I have that feedback.js file in the API folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.26,
          "end": 128.07,
          "en": "in the pages folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.07,
          "end": 131.05,
          "en": "Now that will create a special path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.05,
          "end": 132.86,
          "en": "we can send requests to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.86,
          "end": 136.17000000000002,
          "en": "It will allow us to send requests to our domain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.17000000000002,
          "end": 137.69,
          "en": "So during development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.69,
          "end": 142.69,
          "en": "that's local host 3000/API/feedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.01,
          "end": 146.17000000000002,
          "en": "This is what this will enable us to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.17000000000002,
          "end": 147.54,
          "en": "And that should make sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.54,
          "end": 150.13,
          "en": "because we're in the API folder in the pages folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.13,
          "end": 152.325,
          "en": "and we have a feedback.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.325,
          "end": 154.96,
          "en": "Nonetheless, I mentioned that files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.96,
          "end": 156.786,
          "en": "and folders inside of API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.786,
          "end": 160.03,
          "en": "so inside of this API folder would be treated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.03,
          "end": 162.53,
          "en": "in a special way and they will,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.53,
          "end": 164.35,
          "en": "inside of any file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.35,
          "end": 166.04,
          "en": "inside of the API folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 166.04,
          "end": 168.56,
          "en": "like this feedback.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.56,
          "end": 172.44,
          "en": "we don't export a react component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.44,
          "end": 173.86,
          "en": "So in the upper page files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 173.86,
          "end": 178.86,
          "en": "we do create a react component and export that as a default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 179.12,
          "end": 182.4,
          "en": "We don't do that in API routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.4,
          "end": 185.49,
          "en": "Instead here, we create a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.49,
          "end": 188.81,
          "en": "a function which we typically should name, handler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.81,
          "end": 191.93,
          "en": "because it will handle incoming requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 191.93,
          "end": 195.89,
          "en": "and a function which will get two parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.89,
          "end": 199.12,
          "en": "a request object, which we could name, req",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.12,
          "end": 201.64,
          "en": "and a response object which we could name, res",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.69,
          "end": 205.3,
          "en": "and its dysfunction which we should export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.3,
          "end": 207.41,
          "en": "as a default here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.41,
          "end": 209.98,
          "en": "Now that will not be a react component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.98,
          "end": 213.113,
          "en": "This is a standard Java script function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 214.14,
          "end": 218.12,
          "en": "Now because this file is in the API folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 218.12,
          "end": 223.12,
          "en": "next.js will kind of take this function here to execute it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 223.56,
          "end": 228.56,
          "en": "for incoming requests sent to /API/feedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 229.21,
          "end": 231.25,
          "en": "And the interesting thing is that now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 231.25,
          "end": 233.19,
          "en": "inside of this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 233.19,
          "end": 236.06,
          "en": "we can not just handle get requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 236.06,
          "end": 239.21,
          "en": "and we don't have to send back HTML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 239.21,
          "end": 241.75,
          "en": "Instead, this allows us to execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 241.75,
          "end": 245.29,
          "en": "any server side code of our choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 245.29,
          "end": 248.67,
          "en": "and that's important server side code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 248.67,
          "end": 250.75,
          "en": "Any code we write in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 250.75,
          "end": 255.75,
          "en": "will never end up in any client side code bundle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 255.84,
          "end": 259.46,
          "en": "So any code we write here will never be exposed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 259.46,
          "end": 262.12,
          "en": "to visitors of our webpage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 262.12,
          "end": 264.63,
          "en": "just as code written and getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 265.57,
          "end": 270.08,
          "en": "and getServerProps would never be exposed to our visitors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 270.08,
          "end": 271.27,
          "en": "It's the same here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 271.27,
          "end": 275.13,
          "en": "for these API routes and the code related to them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 275.13,
          "end": 278.21,
          "en": "So here in handler, for a basic start,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 278.21,
          "end": 281.33,
          "en": "we could start sending back a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 281.33,
          "end": 284.77,
          "en": "and we do that with help of that response object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 284.77,
          "end": 289.09000000000003,
          "en": "Now, if you have some node.js or express.js experience,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 289.09000000000003,
          "end": 291.62,
          "en": "this will look very familiar to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 291.62,
          "end": 295.25,
          "en": "And indeed here we will write node.js code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 295.25,
          "end": 300.25,
          "en": "enhanced by the next.js team to look a bit like express.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 300.47,
          "end": 302.66,
          "en": "For example, we can send back a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 302.66,
          "end": 305.13,
          "en": "with help of the response object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 305.13,
          "end": 306.25,
          "en": "And on that object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 306.25,
          "end": 309.21,
          "en": "we can call special methods that allow us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 309.21,
          "end": 313.68,
          "en": "to send back that response and to configure that response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 313.68,
          "end": 316,
          "en": "For example, the status method allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 316,
          "end": 319.4,
          "en": "to set a status code and that could be 200",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 319.4,
          "end": 322.573,
          "en": "for a start to set a success status code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 323.54,
          "end": 327.49,
          "en": "Then on that method, we can chain another method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 327.49,
          "end": 331.4,
          "en": "So call a method on the result of this first method call,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 331.4,
          "end": 334.38,
          "en": "and that could be the JSON method to send back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 334.38,
          "end": 337.74,
          "en": "some JSON data as part of the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 337.74,
          "end": 340.18,
          "en": "for incoming requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 340.18,
          "end": 341.86,
          "en": "And that is quite standard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 341.86,
          "end": 344.47,
          "en": "As I mentioned before, for APIs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 344.47,
          "end": 348.9,
          "en": "you typically exchange data in that JSON format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 348.9,
          "end": 351.1,
          "en": "because it's a highly machine readable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 351.1,
          "end": 353.59000000000003,
          "en": "and also human readable data format,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 353.59000000000003,
          "end": 355.82,
          "en": "which is the defacto standard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 355.82,
          "end": 358.723,
          "en": "for exchanging data with APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 359.89,
          "end": 364.56,
          "en": "Now to the JSON method, we pass a JavaScript value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 364.56,
          "end": 368.48,
          "en": "like an object that will then be transformed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 368.48,
          "end": 370.9,
          "en": "into JSON automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 370.9,
          "end": 373.97,
          "en": "And here we could have a message property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 373.97,
          "end": 375.4,
          "en": "This is up to you though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 375.4,
          "end": 377.28,
          "en": "this entire object is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 377.28,
          "end": 380.25,
          "en": "You can put any data you want in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 380.25,
          "end": 383.933,
          "en": "and the message could be, \"This works\" like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 385.04,
          "end": 388.28,
          "en": "So by adding this line of code in that handler method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 388.28,
          "end": 390.64,
          "en": "which is exported as a default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 390.64,
          "end": 393.9,
          "en": "this will be executed by next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 393.9,
          "end": 398.25,
          "en": "when we send the request to /API/feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 398.25,
          "end": 401.9,
          "en": "and this code will then send back a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 401.9,
          "end": 403.65,
          "en": "clearly not a page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 403.65,
          "end": 406.40999999999997,
          "en": "clearly not an HTML response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 406.40999999999997,
          "end": 408.77,
          "en": "but instead some JSON data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 408.77,
          "end": 412.73,
          "en": "because this response is not intended to be consumed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 412.73,
          "end": 414.85,
          "en": "by entering this in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
